{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1793560000000-engineer-module-pins-r2a.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-17 06:00:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-17 13:00:00 +07\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated)\n# Task: module-pins round 2, COMMIT 1 only (R4 alone): fix the P1 (strip sender admission at lift, refuse carried keys), rename the option, ledger row; uncommitted\nRole: VM Runtime\nImplementers:\n- Model: gpt-6.1-sol | Assigned: 2026-10-17 13:00 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: same slice; Architect found a P1 in the R4 part and gave exact steps\n\nWorktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-pins (branch srvm-module-pins, holds your uncommitted R4 diff of 13 files; keep everything not named below). Read ./collab/*architect-module-pins-review.report.md: Part A findings (P1-1, P2-1, P2-2, P3-1..P3-3) and Part C steps 1-7 (this task = steps 1-7 ONLY; steps 8-16, the carrier/pins, are the NEXT dispatch: do not start them). DO EXACTLY: (1) `install-node` in ucf/rows.cljc dissocs `:yin.admit/id :yin.admit/decision :yin.admit/asserters :yin.admit/address` from `response` BEFORE the cbor/encode check and the row; delete the restore-side dissoc and its comment (~:2233-2237). (2) `check-install!`: add to the existing `:install-response` `and` the clause refusing any carried response key whose namespace is \"yin.admit\" (`:yin.k/undecodable :install-response`). (3) rename the lower option `:yin.k/admitted` to `:yin.k/admitted-modules` in rows.cljc, ucf/holder/export.cljc, rows_support.cljc, rows_test.cljc, rows_custody_test.cljc, holder/export_test.cljc, safepoint_harness_test.cljc, and in every doc amendment you wrote (continuation 7.2/Q3/Q5, transport-tuples, UCF 7.11, linker.dht.md, revisions I-8, known-gaps). Do NOT rename the ledger fact kind or the driver's not-holder answer field that already use `:yin.k/admitted` (ledger.cljc, driver.cljc): grep before replacing. (4) Tests: in rows_test.cljc `carried-install-requires-receiver-admission` keep every assertion and add (a) the decoded wire's root `:install` row slot 3 has none of the four keys, (b) the harness-style relift of the lowered machine equals the wire by root (reuse `canonical-under` or compare the install row), (c) a pack with the four keys spliced into the install row refuses `:yin.k/undecodable :install-response` with zero attaches. In holder/export_test.cljc: a frozen parked-installer whose source install response CARRIED the sender admission record (:yin.admit/* keys; build it explicitly, the shared fixtures have none) rehydrates `:ok` and reproduces the pack byte for byte (the P1-1 regression pin). (5) Mutants, run, record counts, restore byte-for-byte: m1 lift keeps the sender keys; m2 check-install! accepts :yin.admit/* keys; m3 gate bypass (as before). Each must be killed by a named test. (6) Docs per P3-3: reword every \"dropped on restore\" to \"never carried by the lift; a carried one is refused\"; add the known-gaps row for P2-1 (holder driver passes no admitted-modules map; install-child handoff through the driver refuses; P2; closed by the next slice) and put the P3-2 docstring note (name-keyed admission is flat over the tree) in the `lower-task` docstring. (7) `clojure -M:test -e :slow` on the focused namespaces of the previous task plus `yin.vm.ucf.holder.*`, kondo on changed files (0 new), `git diff --check`, then the whole JVM quick tier (unrestricted). NO commit/stage; no src/yang, no test/yang; no fixture or pinned golden may move (if one does, STOP). Report ./collab/<ms>-engineer-module-pins-r2a.report.md with headers, counts, mutants, truthful. End READY or BLOCKED.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
