{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1630,1660p;1830,1875p;2224,2246p;2273,2298p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '1,65p;1367,1425p' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc; sed -n '1,65p;395,515p' test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export_test.cljc; cat collab/1793530000000-engineer-module-pins.prompt.md\"","aggregated_output":"\n\n(declare lift-task*)\n\n\n(defn- install-node\n  [ctx mn inst opts]\n  (let [{:keys [phase parent response]} inst]\n    (when-not (contains? #{:running :parked} phase)\n      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :incomplete-install {:yin.k/name mn :yin.k/phase phase}))\n    (when-not (try (cbor/encode response) true\n                   (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _e false))\n      (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :install-response {:yin.k/name mn}))\n    (node :install [mn phase parent response\n                    (lift-task* (:vm inst) (:serve! ctx)\n                                (assoc (dissoc opts :free-env) :path (conj (:path ctx) mn)) :child)])))\n\n\n(defn- lift-task*\n  [m serve! opts role]\n  (when (seq (:ready-queue m))\n    (outcome! :yin.k/not-quiescent nil {:yin.k/ready (count (:ready-queue m))}))\n  (when-some [h (unliftable-hold m)]\n    (outcome! :yin.k/non-portable :reason-mismatch {:yin.k/hold h}))\n  (when (some? (:control m))\n    (outcome! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint nil {:yin.k/pc (get-in m [:control :pc])}))\n  (let [value (:value m)\n        active? (and (map? value) (= :parked-continuation (:type value)) (contains? (:parked m) (:id value)))\n        kind (cond active? :parked\n                   (seq (:wait-set m)) :blocked\n                   (engine/halted-with-empty-queue? m) :halted\n(defn- check-install!\n  \"One install record: a phase the engine holds a carried child in, the\n   retained response link-install reads (status, manifest naming this\n   module, exports) with the image spawn-child loads, the response's link\n   id equal to the row's parent (the engine settles only the response of\n   its own link), the image the manifest names (continuation §11 Q3: the\n   manifest's :yin.semantic/code derivation record is the response's\n   :derivation, from the manifest's tree to the image's A), and a child\n   that is blocked: the engine links a halted child in the sweep it\n   halts in.\"\n  [recv inst]\n  (let [[mn phase parent response child] (:slots inst)\n        manifest (when (map? response) (:manifest response))\n        child-kind (nth (:slots child) 2)]\n    (when-not (contains? #{:running :parked} phase)\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-phase {:yin.k/name mn :yin.k/phase phase}))\n    (when-not (and (map? response) (= :ok (:status response)) (map? manifest)\n                   (= mn (:yin.module/name manifest))\n                   (coll? (:yin.module/exports manifest)) (every? symbol? (:yin.module/exports manifest))\n                   (map? (:image response)) (attaches? recv (:value (:image response)) nil))\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-response {:yin.k/name mn}))\n    (when-not (and (some? parent) (= parent (:yin.link/id response)))\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-link-id {:yin.k/name mn}))\n    (let [record (:derivation response)]\n      (when-not (and (map? record)\n                     (jing/segment-matches? (get-in manifest [:yin.module/derivations :yin.semantic/code]) record)\n                     (= (:yin.ledger/input record) (:yin.module/tree manifest))\n                     (jing/segment-matches? (:yin.ledger/output record) (:value (:image response))))\n        (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-image {:yin.k/name mn})))\n    (when-not (= :blocked child-kind)\n      (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :install-child {:yin.k/name mn :yin.k/task-kind child-kind}))))\n\n\n(defn- check-pendings!\n  \"Step 8, pending and operations: role, kind, parked id, every :install\n   pending names a carried install, every install record.\"\n  [recv task role]\n  (let [[_ _ kind role' _ _ _ _ parked _ _ _ installs waits parked-id] (:slots task)]\n    (when-not (= role role') (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :role {:yin.k/role role'}))\n    (let [names (into #{} (map #(first (:slots %))) installs)]\n      (doseq [w waits]\n        (let [[reason n] (:slots (second (:slots w)))]\n          (when (and (= :install reason) (not (contains? names n)))\n            (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :incomplete-install {:yin.k/name n})))))\n    (case kind\n      :halted (when (seq waits) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :kind {:yin.k/task-kind kind}))\n                                     [mid (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (value v)])) (partition 2 (:slots s)))])))\n                         module-stores)\n            parked' (into {} (map (fn [[p _]] [p (parked-record p)])) parked-index)\n            entries (mapv entry waits)\n            link (some #(let [[reason _ _ req resp] (:slots (second (:slots %)))]\n                          (when (contains? #{:link-request :link-response} reason) [req resp]))\n                       waits)\n            [base installs'] (reduce (fn [[r acc] inst]\n                                       (let [[mn phase parent response child] (:slots inst)\n                                             ;; Only the receiver's admitted name/address permits\n                                             ;; this child. Drop the sender's decision before\n                                             ;; link-install can publish it as local evidence.\n                                             response (dissoc response :yin.admit/id :yin.admit/decision\n                                                              :yin.admit/asserters :yin.admit/address)\n                                             [spawned r'] (spawn-child r response mn (:fenced? custody))]\n                                         [r' (assoc acc mn {:phase phase :parent parent :response response\n                                                            :vm (restore-task spawned child handles custody false)})]))\n                                     [base {}] installs)\n            fe (keyed free-env)\n            resources (merge (:resources base)\n                             (into {} (map (fn [[identity k]] [k (get handles identity)])) stream-keys)\n                             (into {} (map (fn [[c body]]\n                                             [(get cell-keys c) {:stream-id (stream-key (first (:slots body)))\n(defn lower-task\n  \"The lower of §7.2 into recv, a fresh semantic machine of the\n   receiver's composition: gate to frames (decode) and the store keys,\n   then pendings and install records, dependency closure (code, closures,\n   primitives), each step over the whole tree before the next, then\n   custody (check-custody!), all before the first attach! (step 11); then\n   restore (step 12), which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the\n   restored machine, or throws the first refusal as ex-data.\n   opts: :budget; :yin.k/admitted, a composition-supplied {name manifest-address}\n   for carried install children (default empty, fail closed; carried admission\n   evidence is dropped); :exclusive, refuse a fork root; :grant and :protection,\n   required by a blocked or parked exclusive root (handoff.cljc's reader\n   contract: the grant names :checkpoint, the pack address, its lease,\n   holder, tenure and evidence; :protection maps every stream identity of\n   the tree to its class); :fenced, an administrative rehydration that\n   skips the grant and restores every task of the tree gated :exporting,\n   its waits in :yin.k/recovery-waits and its parked records in\n   :yin.k/recovery-parked (none in the scheduler), its id counter the\n   carried one exactly and :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids mapping each cursor\n   cell's resource key to its carried cell id.\"\n  ([recv wire attach!] (lower-task recv wire attach! {}))\n  ([recv wire attach! opts]\n   (let [task (decode wire (merge default-budget (:budget opts)))]\n     (when-not (= :task (:kind task)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :root {}))\n     ;; each step over the whole tree before the next (§3.3)\n     (doseq [step [check-stores! check-pendings! check-dependencies!]\n(ns yin.vm.ucf.rows-test\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [dao.jing.cbor-fixtures :as fx]\n            [yang.python.antlr.int-contract-fixtures :as ints]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as support]\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n            [yin.vm.semantic.frame-test :as ft]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.malformed-rows :as malformed]))\n\n\n(defn error\n  [f]\n  (try (f) nil (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-data e))))\n\n\n(defn task-node\n  [cursor-cells result]\n  (rows/node :task [3 rows/profile :halted :root 0 (rows/node :bindings [])\n                    (rows/node :store []) [] (rows/node :parked-table [])\n                    (rows/node :cursor-cells (mapcat identity cursor-cells)) {} {} [] [] nil result nil]))\n\n\n(defn cursor-cell-body\n  [stream position]\n  (rows/node :cursor-cell-body [(rows/node :stream [stream {:peer stream}]) position]))\n\n\n(defn fixture\n  [a b x y]\n  (let [payload [:row (rows/node :map\n                                 [[:lit 'both] [:row (rows/node :set [[:cursor-cell x] [:cursor-cell y]])]\n                                  [:lit 'one] [:cursor-cell x]\n                                  [:lit 'streams] [:row (rows/node :set [[:row (rows/node :stream [a {:peer a}])]\n                                                                         [:row (rows/node :stream [b {:peer b}])]])]\n                                  [:lit 'cursors] [:row (rows/node :map [[:cursor-cell x] [:lit :x] [:cursor-cell y] [:lit :y]])]])]\n        task (task-node [[x (cursor-cell-body a 0)] [y (cursor-cell-body b 0)]] [:lit nil])]\n    (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots task) 6 (rows/node :store ['payload payload])))))\n\n\n(declare portable-frame)\n\n\n(defn- encoded\n  [x]\n  (cond (and (map? x) (contains? x :yin.k/row)) [:row (:yin.k/row x)]\n        (and (map? x) (contains? x :yin.k/cursor-cell)) [:cursor-cell (:yin.k/cursor-cell x)]\n        :else [:lit x]))\n\n\n(defn- portable-value\n  [m x]\n  ;; Classify native test values into the decoded codec domain. No seals\n  ;; travel. Captures retain their entire act and K; closures retain the\n  ;; code address, binders, lexical bindings and module context.\n  (cond\n    (values/continuation? x)\n    {:yin.k/row (rows/node :reified\n     :cljd (println \"SKIP host-collapse: slash-crossed identifiers remain distinct on Dart\")))\n\n\n(deftest carried-install-requires-receiver-admission\n  (let [sender-record {:yin.admit/id \"sender-only\"\n                       :yin.admit/decision :allow\n                       :yin.admit/asserters #{'sender}\n                       :yin.admit/address :sender-only}\n        source (update-in (support/parked-installer)\n                          [:installs 'host.mod :response] merge sender-record)\n        wire (support/lift source nil)\n        address (jing/segment-key (:manifest (support/module-response)))\n        recv (support/new-machine)]\n    (doseq [opts [{} {:yin.k/admitted {'other.mod address}}\n                  {:yin.k/admitted {'host.mod :wrong-address}}\n                  {:yin.k/admitted {'host.mod nil}}]]\n      (let [{:keys [attach! count]} (support/attacher)\n            refusal (error #(rows/lower-task recv wire attach! opts))]\n        (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied (:yin.k/status refusal)))\n        (is (= {:yin.k/modules {'host.mod address}} (:yin.k/missing refusal)))\n        (is (zero? @count))\n        (is (empty? (:installs recv)))))\n    (let [{:keys [attach! count]} (support/attacher)\n          restored (rows/lower-task (assoc recv :attach-stream attach!) wire attach! {:yin.k/admitted {'host.mod address}})\n          response (get-in restored [:installs 'host.mod :response])\n          child (get-in restored [:installs 'host.mod :vm])\n          wait (first (:wait-set child))]\n      (is (pos? @count))\n      (is (not-any? #(contains? response %) (keys sender-record)))\n      (stream/append! (get (:resources child) (:stream-id wait)) :resume)\n      (let [done (vm/run restored)\n            installed (module/module-entry (:modules (:modules done)) 'host.mod)]\n        (is (= 42 (:value done)))\n        (is (= address (:address installed)))\n        (is (not (contains? installed :admission)))))))\n(ns yin.vm.ucf.holder.export-test\n  \"D8 over the row carrier (UCF 7.7.4; r3 1.8 and 1.9; phase 7b): the\n   exporting state, the prepare/encode split over rows/lift-task, the\n   export-recovery object version 2, its fenced rehydration and the abort\n   rule. Every machine is a semantic machine the real engine\n   parked (yin.vm.ucf.rows-support); counting handles show what the gate,\n   the encode and the rehydration touch.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.ringbuffer :as ringbuffer]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.holder.export :as export]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows-support :as rs]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Machines, the exporter, the receiver's attach\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- throws?\n  [thunk]\n  (try (thunk) false\n       (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _ true)))\n\n\n(defn- ring\n  [capacity]\n  (:dao.stream/handle\n    (ringbuffer/create! {:dao.stream/type ringbuffer/transport-type\n                         ringbuffer/capacity-key capacity})))\n\n\n(defn- index\n  \"The composition's source index, as the composition reads it.\"\n  []\n  @rs/source-index)\n\n\n(defn- two-streams\n  \"Parks on a read of the first stream; the store also holds the second\n   stream and a cursor on each, so the lift reaches two streams.\"\n  []\n  (rs/let1 'a {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n           (rs/let1 'b {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}\n                    (rs/then (rs/def! 'held-a (rs/cursor-of (rs/v 'a)))\n                             (rs/then (rs/def! 'held-b (rs/cursor-of (rs/v 'b)))\n                                      (rs/next-of (rs/v 'held-a)))))))\n\n\n(defn- parked-machine\n  []\n  (vm/run (rs/load-ast (rs/new-machine) (two-streams))))\n\n\n(defn- served-table\n  \"A `serve!` that counts its calls and answers one stable identity per\n   handle.\"\n  []\n                 (compare-and-set! first-handle nil h)\n                 (when (= h @first-handle) served-answer))\n        refused (export/prepare m' record stingy nil (index))]\n    (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied (:yin.k/status refused)) (pr-str refused))\n    (is (= 1 (count (get-in refused [:record :served]))))\n    (testing \"a retry with the returned record never re-serves that stream\"\n      (let [asked (atom [])\n            {:keys [serve!]} (served-table)\n            retry (export/prepare m' (:record refused)\n                                  (fn [h]\n                                    (swap! asked conj h)\n                                    (serve! h))\n                                  nil (index))]\n        (is (= :ok (:status retry)) (pr-str retry))\n        (is (not-any? #(= @first-handle %) @asked))\n        (is (= 1 (count @asked)) \"only the other stream\")))))\n\n\n(deftest a-custody-refusal-after-the-walk-keeps-what-the-walk-served-test\n  ;; phase-7a D4: the row lift serves while it walks and decides the\n  ;; protection and exhaustion refusals after; the record accounts for it\n  (doseq [[label header expected]\n          [[\"an enrolled write without an operation id\"\n            (rs/header 0 rs/origin #{\"s0\"}) :unprotected-pending]\n           [\"an exhausted counter\"\n            (rs/header rows/max-exact rs/origin #{}) :op-seq-exhausted]]]\n    (testing label\n      (let [{m :machine record :record} (export/enter (rs/parked-writer))\n            {:keys [calls serve!]} (served-table)\n            refused (export/prepare m record serve! header (index))\n            served @calls]\n        (is (= :yin.k/non-portable (:yin.k/status refused)) (pr-str refused))\n        (is (= expected (:yin.k/kind refused)))\n        (is (pos? served) \"the walk served before the refusal\")\n        (is (= served (count (get-in refused [:record :served]))) \"and the record retains every answer\")\n        (export/prepare m (:record refused) serve! header (index))\n        (is (= served @calls) \"a retry serves nothing twice\")))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Freeze: recovery version 2\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest the-recovery-object-is-the-pack-and-holder-local-state-test\n  (let [{:keys [frozen prepared machine]} (frozen-of (rs/parked-explicit))\n        recovery (cbor/decode (:bytes frozen))\n        published (export/encode machine (:record prepared))]\n    (is (= :ok (:status frozen)) (pr-str frozen))\n    (is (= #{:yin.k/export-recovery :yin.k/version :yin.k/pack-address :yin.k/root\n             :yin.k/pack-bytes :yin.k/header :yin.k/state}\n           (set (keys recovery)))\n        \"one body: no snapshot, no descriptors (the pack carries them)\")\n    (is (= 2 (:yin.k/version recovery)))\n    (is (= (:address published) (:pack-address frozen) (:yin.k/pack-address recovery)))\n    (is (= (:root published) (:root frozen) (:yin.k/root recovery)))\n    (is (= (vec (:bytes published)) (vec (:pack-bytes frozen))\n           (vec (jing/base64->bytes (:yin.k/pack-bytes recovery)))))\n    (is (jing/segment-bytes-match? (:address frozen) (:bytes frozen)))\n    (is (= #{:gate :origins :issues :issued :children} (set (keys (:yin.k/state recovery)))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Rehydrate: fenced, reproducible, without program IO\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(deftest complete-export-recovery-is-fenced-and-reproducible-test\n  (doseq [[label source header] [[\"a parked reader\" (rs/parked-reader) nil]\n                                 [\"an explicit park\" (rs/parked-explicit) nil]\n                                 [\"an installer\" (rs/parked-installer) nil]\n                                 [\"a parked reader under a header\" (rs/parked-reader) (rs/header 0 nil #{})]\n                                 [\"a halted root under a header\" (rs/halted-machine) (rs/header 0 rs/origin #{})]]]\n    (testing label\n      (let [{:keys [frozen record prepared]} (frozen-of source header)\n            {:keys [attaches calls attach]} (counting-attach)\n            restored (rehydrate frozen (rs/new-machine) attach)]\n        (is (= :ok (:status frozen)) (pr-str frozen))\n        (is (= :ok (:status restored)) (pr-str restored))\n        (is (= :exporting (vm/gate-mode (:machine restored))))\n        (is (empty? (:wait-set (:machine restored))))\n        (is (empty? (:parked (:machine restored))))\n        (is (= (count (:wait-set record)) (count (get-in restored [:record :wait-set]))))\n        (is (= (set (keys (:parked record))) (set (keys (get-in restored [:record :parked])))))\n        (is (nil? (get-in restored [:machine :yin.k/custody])) \"no custody is restored\")\n        (is (zero? @calls) \"no read, write, mint or close\")\n        (is (= (count (into #{} (map :dao.stream/identity) (vals (get-in prepared [:record :served]))))\n               @attaches)\n            \"every stream attached, once\")\n        (is (reproduces? frozen restored) \"the published pack, byte for byte\")))))\n\n\n(deftest recovery-requires-receiver-install-admission-test\n  (let [{:keys [frozen]} (frozen-of (rs/parked-installer))\n        address (jing/segment-key (:manifest (rs/module-response)))]\n    (doseq [admitted [nil {'host.mod :wrong-address}]]\n      (let [{:keys [attaches attach]} (counting-attach)\n            refused (export/rehydrate-fenced\n                      (rs/new-machine) (:bytes frozen)\n                      {:address (:address frozen) :attach attach\n                       :yin.k/admitted admitted})]\n        (is (= :yin.k/unsatisfied (:yin.k/status refused)))\n        (is (= {:yin.k/modules {'host.mod address}} (:yin.k/missing refused)))\n        (is (zero? @attaches))))))\n\n\n(deftest a-restarted-abort-is-refused-test\n  (let [{:keys [frozen]} (frozen-of (rs/parked-reader))\n        restored (rehydrate frozen)]\n    (is (= :ok (:status restored)) (pr-str restored))\n    (is (true? (get-in restored [:record :recovered?])))\n    (is (= [:yin.k/refused :restarted]\n           ((juxt :yin.k/status :yin.k/reason)\n            (export/abort (:machine restored) (:record restored) [] nil))))))\n\n\n(deftest recovery-restores-fresh-name-state-without-receiver-contamination-test\n  (let [source (assoc (rs/parked-reader) :origins 42 :id-counter 88 :yin.k/issued 77)\n        {:keys [frozen]} (frozen-of source)\n        restored (rehydrate frozen\n                            (assoc (rs/new-machine) :origins 99 :id-counter 100\n                                   :store {'receiver-local :wrong} :yin.k/issued 33\n                                   :yin.k/closes [{:receiver-local true}])\nCreated-GMT: 2026-10-17 04:00:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-17 11:00:00 +07\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated)\n# Task: module-identity pins on the row carrier + receiver-side re-check + carried install children admitted by the receiver (Architect threat model verdict \"C\" + R4), uncommitted\nRole: VM Runtime\nImplementers:\n- Model: gpt-6.1-sol | Assigned: 2026-10-17 11:00 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: owner said \"dispatch it to codex\"; Architect (Fable) reviews before any commit; this is a security-relevant format change\n\nWorktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-pins (branch srvm-module-pins @ origin/master). Read COMPLETELY: ./collab/*architect-fetch-threat-model.report.md (the Architect's threat model; sections 3 (routes R1-R13), 4.1-4.5, 5, 6 verdict, 7 tests and docs) and ./collab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md row on Q5. IMPLEMENT the verdict: (1) CARRIER: the task row's `requires` carries `:yin.k/modules {module-name manifest-address-or-nil}` (UCF section 7.6.4 form): the lift keeps the registry entry's `:address` for every registry-answered namespaced free name that discharge! answers via the registry (rows.cljc ~:1615-1617; a host-registered module has no address: nil, satisfied only by a host module of that name with equal export profiles via module/host-export-profile). Update the row grammar tables (docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md section 5.x, UCF 7.6.4/7.6.5 pointers), the row encoder/decoder and validators, restore. Packs re-mint: regenerate test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/rows-checkpoint-v3.txt via the existing rows-checkpoint-fixtures/render route (see how 9ab9e792 did it) and record a dated entry in docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md (I-8); no backward compatibility is owed. (2) LOWER re-check (B): `check-dependencies!` (rows.cljc ~:1898) re-discharges registry-answered names against the RECEIVER's registry by EQUAL ADDRESS (not name presence): a missing or different module refuses BEFORE attach with the exact outcome of section 4.2 (`:yin.k/unsatisfied`, `:yin.k/discovery :complete`, `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {...} :obligations #{...}}`), kind `:module-pin-mismatch` naming both addresses when the receiver holds a different address (words of engine.cljc:1388-1393 `:dependency-pin-mismatch`). The lower stays pure over the receiver value and attaches nothing on refusal (attach-count law); the receiver's registry is still kept as given. (3) R4: carried `:install` children: the lower refuses a child unless its manifest address is in a composition-supplied opts set `{:yin.k/admitted {name address}}` (default empty = fail closed), as `:yin.k/unsatisfied {:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {name carried-address}}}` before any attach (section 4.4); and at `link-install` (engine.cljc ~:1436-1443) the copied sender `:admission` record must not stand for the receiver's decision: replace it by the receiver's (opts-supplied) record or drop it, as the report specifies. (4) Documentation: continuation 2.5 and 7.2 (the lower now re-discharges registry names by pinned address; Q5 answered C), UCF 7.11, the refusal shape, and the FORBIDDEN list for a composition's fetch loop (section 4.2 last bullet, section 5) in the right design doc; update docs/agents/known-gaps.md rows (Q5, R4 install-child admission). The fetch LOOP itself is NOT part of this slice (composition policy; no fetch code in the VM or lower; do not add one). TESTS (portable .cljc, section 7.1): pin equal-address satisfaction, different-address refusal naming both addresses, missing-module refusal before attach with attach-count zero, host-module nil pin with equal and unequal profiles, install child refused with empty admitted set and accepted when listed, `link-install` no longer copies the sender's admission, the decoded pack round-trips the new slot, malformed slot refused (add to malformed_rows UCF collection like the :equality-collapse entry), and a mutant for each (name-only satisfaction regress: test fails). RULES: no src/yang, no test/yang, no collab commits, no `--yolo`; if any pinned A address, descriptor hash or golden other than rows fixtures carrying requires/install moves, STOP and report old/new; if the spec in the report is ambiguous or you need a decision (e.g. where the host-module profile is recorded), STOP that sub-part and report; never weaken an assertion; no commit/stage. Foreground lanes: kondo on changed files (0 new); focused `clojure -M:test -e :slow -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-custody-test -n yin.vm.ucf.rows-checkpoint-test -n yin.vm.ucf.remote-test -n yin.vm.semantic.safepoint-harness-test -n yin.vm.semantic.frame-test -n yin.vm.linker-test -n yin.vm.linker-manifest-test -n yin.vm.mint-test -n yin.vm.semantic.layout-test` and `-r '^dao\\.jing\\..*'`; then the whole JVM quick tier `clojure -M:test -e :slow` (unrestricted; `bb gen:python-antlr` first if the lexer is missing). No Node/Dart (orchestrator). Report ./collab/<ms>-engineer-module-pins.report.md with Completed-GMT/Completed-Local/Coding-Agent/Session-ID: per-part what changed, fixtures moved (old/new addresses), counts, mutants, what you STOPPED on, file-to-commit mapping (code / tests / docs), truthful. End READY or BLOCKED.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
