{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'canonical-under|defn lift|defn lower|rows/encode|update-in.*slots.*12' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_support.cljc; sed -n '1810,1830p;2755,2767p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; sed -n '413,426p' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md; sed -n '2330,2342p' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md; sed -n '714,730p' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md; rg -n 'defn.*reproduces|defn.*rehydrate|defn.*frozen-of' test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export_test.cljc; rg -n ':yin.k/admitted' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/{holder/ledger,holder/driver}.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'canonical-under|defn lift|defn lower|rows/encode|update-in.*slots.*12' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_support.cljc; sed -n '1810,1830p;2755,2767p' docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md; sed -n '413,426p' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md; sed -n '2330,2342p' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md; sed -n '714,730p' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md; rg -n 'defn.*reproduces|defn.*rehydrate|defn.*frozen-of' test/yin/vm/ucf/holder/export_test.cljc; rg -n ':yin.k/admitted' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/{holder/ledger,holder/driver}.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_support.cljc:359:(defn lift-opts\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_support.cljc:366:(defn lift\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:178:(deftest canonical-under-is-renaming-invariant\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:181:        ca (rows/canonical-under a {:lane-a/s1 :s1 :lane-a/s2 :s2})\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:182:        cb (rows/canonical-under b {:lane-b/s2 :s1 :lane-b/s1 :s2})]\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:185:           (:yin.k/root (rows/canonical-under\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:191:           (:yin.k/kind (error #(rows/canonical-under a {:lane-a/s1 :s1})))))))\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:300:    (is (= (:yin.k/root (rows/canonical-under wire {:child/s :child :root/s :root}))\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:301:           (:yin.k/root (rows/emit (rows/decode (rows/canonical-under wire {:child/s :child :root/s :root}))))))))\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:355:    (is (= (:yin.k/root (rows/canonical-under (rows/emit a) ident))\ntest/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc:356:           (:yin.k/root (rows/canonical-under (rows/emit b) ident))))))\n| custody | `check-custody!` | `custody-baseline` over the tree; fork refused under `:exclusive`; halted exclusive needs no grant; blocked/parked exclusive validates grant evidence, pack checkpoint, binding, lease/holder, arbitration, epoch, live tenure and input prefix, then protection in both directions and op-id presence against enrollment; `:fenced` skips grant/protection | grammar's `:yin.k/undecodable` kinds; `:yin.k/profile-mismatch`, `:yin.k/awaiting-grant`, `:yin.k/not-holder`, `:yin.k/unsatisfied` |\n\n**Amended 2026-10-16 (module-pins, R4).** After custody validation and\nbefore attachment, every carried install child must have its manifest\naddress listed under its module name in the receiving composition's\n`opts {:yin.k/admitted {name manifest-address}}`. The default is empty:\nan absent or different address refuses as\n`{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied\n  :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {name carried-address}}}`.\nThis applies to children throughout the task tree, including fenced\nrestoration; `holder.export/rehydrate-fenced` forwards the composition's\n`:yin.k/admitted` option to the lower. Restore drops the sender's\n`:yin.admit/id`, `:yin.admit/decision`,\n`:yin.admit/asserters` and `:yin.admit/address` from each retained install\nresponse before `link-install` can record them as receiver evidence. The\ncomposition supplies admissions from its own policy, never from the pack.\n\nThen **attachment** (step 11, `attach-streams!`): one `attach!` per\ndistinct stream identity of the whole tree, `:yin.k/unsatisfied\n{:dao.stream/identity …}` when the composition declines. Then **restore**\n(step 12, `restore-task`): the carried vectors attached by A into a\n  shape, image admission and blocked child, then requires a non-nil parent\n  equal to response `:yin.link/id`. The manifest's semantic derivation\n  address must hash the response's derivation record; its input equals\n  the manifest tree and its output equals the image vector's A.\n  This verifies response self-consistency. Amended 2026-10-16 (R4): the\n  lower additionally requires the receiver composition's explicit\n  `:yin.k/admitted {name manifest-address}` before attaching any stream,\n  and drops the sender's admission evidence on restore.\n- **Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)** — Reason: 7a implements the op-id grammar; correlation checks remain narrower.\n  **6b Q4, CLOSED for operation ids; correlation agreement remains open.**\n  `custody-baseline` checks retained put/FFI-request/link-request ids\n  throughout the tree: exact sequences below next-op-seq, uniqueness,\n  origin required, and no id naming the root's own occurrence. Fork trees\n**Amended 2026-10-16 (R4).** Self-consistency does not admit a carried\nchild into the receiver's installation family. Before any stream attach,\nthe lower additionally requires the receiving composition's opts\n`:yin.k/admitted {name manifest-address}` to list the child's manifest\naddress under its name. Default empty refuses with\n`{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied\n  :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {name carried-address}}}`. Restore drops\nthe sender's four `:yin.admit/*` decision fields from the retained\nresponse before `link-install` can record them on the receiver's entry.\nThis changes admission behavior, not the `:install` row's slots.\nA remains the only code identity and the Universal AST is never lost.\nNo new resolver or independent claimed-image-address check is added.\n\n### 5.5 The root\n**Amended 2026-10-16 (carried install children, R4).** A lowered pack's\ninstall child enters this family only when the receiving composition\nexplicitly admits its name and manifest address through lower opts\n`:yin.k/admitted`. The lower refuses unlisted or differently addressed\nchildren before any stream attachment, including during fenced restore.\nSender admission fields are dropped from the retained response; they do\nnot become the receiving registry entry's `:admission`.\n\nThe exposure domain is therefore the installation family for its life,\nnot one task. It is about principal plus address plus holder context,\nand it is language-blind: any frontend compiling to a require of that\nname hits the same entry.\n\n**2026-10-16, I-8 (module-pins slice, partial; R4 only).** Lower now\nrequires composition-supplied `:yin.k/admitted {name manifest-address}`\nfor every carried install child, default empty, before attaching streams;\nrestore drops the sender's admission decision fields. No row shape or\nfixture address changes in this partial slice. The module-pin carrier,\nhost-profile schema and their fixture re-mint are blocked pending the\nArchitect's decision on where host-module export profiles are recorded.\nNo compatibility promise is added.\n124:(defn- frozen-of\n136:(defn- rehydrate\n144:(defn- reproduces?\nrg: src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/ledger.cljc: No such file or directory (os error 2)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc:743:             :yin.k/admitted (:yin.k/variants entry)}\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/holder/driver.cljc:1655:                  :yin.k/admitted (:yin.k/variants entry)} l)\n","exit_code":2,"status":"failed"}}
